            <ArticleTitle>[Pain sensitivity during chronic psychoemotional stress in humans].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>337-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a natural &quot;model&quot; of a chronic psychoemotional stress in humans, (neurasthenia) a decrease in the nociceptive threshold was found. The decrease resulting from weakening of supraspinal tonic descending inhibition which, in its turn, evidently was due to a diminished activity (or dysfunction) of the brain opioid system occurring in a long-lasting psychoemotional stress.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
